Azure Virtual Machine in Availability Zone 1

## Overview
This project creates a Linux Virtual Machine in **Availability Zone 1** on Microsoft Azure. An Availability Zone is a separate datacenter inside an Azure region, with its own power, cooling and network. Placing a VM in a zone protects it from a single datacenter failure.

--- An Availability Zone (AZ) is a physically separate datacenter inside one Azure region. Each zone has its own power, cooling, and networking. Most regions that support zones have three: Zone 1, Zone 2, and Zone 3.
--- When you create a VM in Zone 1, Azure places it in that specific datacenter. If you also put a second VM in Zone 2, one datacenter failure will not take down your whole application.
